        {
            "key": "pp_faqs",
            "scope": "pre-press-service",
            "items": [
                [
                    "What are pre-press services?",
                    "Pre-press services involve preparing digital artwork for printing through processes such as file verification, colour management, proofing, layout validation, and print optimization. This ensures every file is technically ready before production begins."
                ],
                [
                    "What is included in professional pre-press services?",
                    "Artwork review, file preparation (resolution, fonts, bleed, colour profiles, overprinting and trapping), proofing and quality checks, print optimization, client review and approval, and production-ready delivery."
                ],
                [
                    "How long does the pre-press process take?",
                    "The timeline depends on the number of files and how much preparation each one needs. It is agreed with you before work begins, together with the scope and pricing."
                ],
                [
                    "What software is used for pre-press?",
                    "We work with Adobe Illustrator, InDesign, Photoshop and Acrobat Pro, Esko ArtPro+ and Automation Engine, GMG colour management, and Enfocus PitStop Pro."
                ],
                [
                    "What industries use pre-press services?",
                    "Any business that prints: packaging and label printers, commercial print, marketing collateral, brochures and wide-format display work."
                ],
                [
                    "Do I need pre-press services for digital printing?",
                    "Yes. Colour shifts, low-resolution images, missing fonts and incorrect layouts cause problems in digital printing too. A pre-press check catches them before the first page is printed."
                ]
            ]
        },
